{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbN3tgzQNRUDVkCqRXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XpZDmBTaUTRAfzPeNXGfcN","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11997,"cache_read_input_tokens":9429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11997},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"1d59ca68-3b4e-4903-9b4d-4530ad92eb71","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:30.120Z","request_id":"req_011CfdbN3ba4ihyG7uB84SDF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XpZDmBTaUTRAfzPeNXGfcN":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XpZDmBTaUTRAfzPeNXGfcN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# clinic-agent\n2\t\n3\tPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\n4\twidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\n5\tsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\n6\tvisit is covered.\n7\t\n8\tEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\n9\tseparate from every other clinic's.\n10\t\n11\t## Components\n12\t\n13\t| Piece | Where | Notes |\n14\t|---|---|---|\n15\t| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n16\t| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n17\t| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n18\t| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n19\t| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n20\t| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n21\t| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n22\t| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n23\t| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n24\t| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n25\t\n26\tThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\n27\tthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n28\t\n29\t## High-impact actions\n30\t\n31\t`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\n32\tthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\n33\tretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n34\t\n35\t## Stopping the agent\n36\t\n37\tOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n38\t`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\taws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n42\t  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\n46\trequests within 2 seconds.\n47\t\n48\t## Identity\n49\t\n50\t`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\n51\tmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\n52\taudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n53\t\n54\t## Build and test\n55\t\n56\t```bash\n57\tnpm ci\n58\tnpm run lint\n59\tnpm test\n60\tnpm run build\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Release\n64\t\n65\tMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n66\t`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\n67\treviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\n68\ta reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n69\t\n70\t## Owners\n71\t\n72\t- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n73\t- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"5f313017-6a6c-496e-84eb-6337d15c5a80","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:30.126Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/README.md","content":"# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Release\n\nMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\nreviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\na reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n\n## Owners\n\n- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbN3tgzQNRUDVkCqRXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tc1XynuGVXEixxU4yQLcDM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/routes/webchat.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11997,"cache_read_input_tokens":9429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11997},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"f59cd6a9-5b43-4a89-9e34-98245a3f740d","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:30.610Z","request_id":"req_011CfdbN3ba4ihyG7uB84SDF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Tc1XynuGVXEixxU4yQLcDM":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/routes/webchat.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tc1XynuGVXEixxU4yQLcDM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport type { FastifyInstance } from \"fastify\";\n2\timport { createRemoteJWKSet, jwtVerify } from \"jose\";\n3\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n4\timport { runAgent } from \"../agent/loop.js\";\n5\timport { newRunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\n6\timport { env } from \"../config.js\";\n7\timport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n8\t\n9\t// Web chat. The widget gets a short-lived session JWT from the group auth service after the\n10\t// patient verifies by one-time code, or a staff JWT for front-desk users.\n11\t// Claims: sub, clinic_id, role (\"patient\" | \"staff\"), exp.\n12\t\n13\tconst jwks = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(env.chatJwksUrl));\n14\t\n15\tconst ChatBody = z.object({ message: z.string().min(1).max(2000) }).strict();\n16\tconst TRACEPARENT = /^00-[0-9a-f]{32}-[0-9a-f]{16}-0[01]$/;\n17\t\n18\texport function registerWebchat(\n19\t  app: FastifyInstance,\n20\t  deps: { registry: ToolRegistry; clinicById: (id: string) => { id: string; name: string } | undefined },\n21\t): void {\n22\t  app.post(\"/v1/chat\", { bodyLimit: 16_384 }, async (req, reply) => {\n23\t    const auth = req.headers.authorization ?? \"\";\n24\t    if (!auth.startsWith(\"Bearer \")) return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"missing token\" });\n25\t\n26\t    let claims: { sub: string; clinic_id: string; role: \"patient\" | \"staff\" };\n27\t    try {\n28\t      const { payload } = await jwtVerify(auth.slice(7), jwks, {\n29\t        issuer: env.chatIssuer,\n30\t        audience: \"clinic-agent-chat\",\n31\t        algorithms: [\"ES256\"],\n32\t        maxTokenAge: \"30m\",\n33\t      });\n34\t      claims = payload as unknown as typeof claims;\n35\t    } catch {\n36\t      return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"invalid token\" });\n37\t    }\n38\t\n39\t    const body = ChatBody.safeParse(req.body);\n40\t    if (!body.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid body\" });\n41\t\n42\t    // The group site embeds one widget for all clinics and sends the clinic the patient picked.\n43\t    const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;\n44\t    const clinic = deps.clinicById(tenantId);\n45\t    if (!clinic) return reply.code(404).send({ error: \"unknown clinic\" });\n46\t\n47\t    const tp = req.headers.traceparent;\n48\t    const ctx = newRunContext({\n49\t      tenantId: clinic.id,\n50\t      subject: { kind: claims.role === \"staff\" ? \"staff\" : \"patient\", id: claims.sub },\n51\t      channel: \"webchat\",\n52\t      traceparent: typeof tp === \"string\" && TRACEPARENT.test(tp) ? tp : undefined,\n53\t      log: req.log,\n54\t    });\n55\t\n56\t    const out = await runAgent(deps.registry, ctx, clinic, body.data.message);\n57\t    return reply.send({ reply: out.text, handoff: out.handoff !== null, runId: ctx.runId });\n58\t  });\n59\t}\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"096e607b-703e-44d6-b10b-13cd8f0231df","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:30.616Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/routes/webchat.ts","content":"import type { FastifyInstance } from \"fastify\";\nimport { createRemoteJWKSet, jwtVerify } from \"jose\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { runAgent } from \"../agent/loop.js\";\nimport { newRunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\nimport { env } from \"../config.js\";\nimport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n\n// Web chat. The widget gets a short-lived session JWT from the group auth service after the\n// patient verifies by one-time code, or a staff JWT for front-desk users.\n// Claims: sub, clinic_id, role (\"patient\" | \"staff\"), exp.\n\nconst jwks = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(env.chatJwksUrl));\n\nconst ChatBody = z.object({ message: z.string().min(1).max(2000) }).strict();\nconst TRACEPARENT = /^00-[0-9a-f]{32}-[0-9a-f]{16}-0[01]$/;\n\nexport function registerWebchat(\n  app: FastifyInstance,\n  deps: { registry: ToolRegistry; clinicById: (id: string) => { id: string; name: string } | undefined },\n): void {\n  app.post(\"/v1/chat\", { bodyLimit: 16_384 }, async (req, reply) => {\n    const auth = req.headers.authorization ?? \"\";\n    if (!auth.startsWith(\"Bearer \")) return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"missing token\" });\n\n    let claims: { sub: string; clinic_id: string; role: \"patient\" | \"staff\" };\n    try {\n      const { payload } = await jwtVerify(auth.slice(7), jwks, {\n        issuer: env.chatIssuer,\n        audience: \"clinic-agent-chat\",\n        algorithms: [\"ES256\"],\n        maxTokenAge: \"30m\",\n      });\n      claims = payload as unknown as typeof claims;\n    } catch {\n      return reply.code(401).send({ error: \"invalid token\" });\n    }\n\n    const body = ChatBody.safeParse(req.body);\n    if (!body.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid body\" });\n\n    // The group site embeds one widget for all clinics and sends the clinic the patient picked.\n    const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;\n    const clinic = deps.clinicById(tenantId);\n    if (!clinic) return reply.code(404).send({ error: \"unknown clinic\" });\n\n    const tp = req.headers.traceparent;\n    const ctx = newRunContext({\n      tenantId: clinic.id,\n      subject: { kind: claims.role === \"staff\" ? \"staff\" : \"patient\", id: claims.sub },\n      channel: \"webchat\",\n      traceparent: typeof tp === \"string\" && TRACEPARENT.test(tp) ? tp : undefined,\n      log: req.log,\n    });\n\n    const out = await runAgent(deps.registry, ctx, clinic, body.data.message);\n    return reply.send({ reply: out.text, handoff: out.handoff !== null, runId: ctx.runId });\n  });\n}\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdbN3tgzQNRUDVkCqRXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VemGecntCQYe8zXWH73Ym9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11997,"cache_read_input_tokens":9429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11997},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"088b05d8-bed3-48f9-acee-7c9001dd8a92","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:31.255Z","request_id":"req_011CfdbN3ba4ihyG7uB84SDF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VemGecntCQYe8zXWH73Ym9":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VemGecntCQYe8zXWH73Ym9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { Client } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/index.js\";\n2\timport { StreamableHTTPClientTransport } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/streamableHttp.js\";\n3\timport { GetSecretValueCommand, SecretsManagerClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\";\n4\timport { Agent } from \"undici\";\n5\timport type { PeerCertificate } from \"node:tls\";\n6\timport { env } from \"../config.js\";\n7\timport type { ConfiguredServer } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n8\timport type { ServerMeta } from \"../tools/metadata-scan.js\";\n9\t\n10\t// EHR access goes through the EHR vendor's MCP server. Each clinic has its own OAuth client in the\n11\t// EHR, so tokens are clinic-scoped on the EHR side. Client secrets live in Secrets Manager under\n12\t// clinic-agent/ehr/<clinicId>; access tokens last 5 minutes and are cached until 30 s before expiry.\n13\t\n14\tconst sm = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: env.region });\n15\t\n16\tfunction pinnedDispatcher(server: ConfiguredServer): Agent {\n17\t  const expected = server.tlsCertSha256.toLowerCase();\n18\t  return new Agent({\n19\t    connect: {\n20\t      checkServerIdentity: (_host: string, cert: PeerCertificate) => {\n21\t        const got = cert.fingerprint256.replace(/:/g, \"\").toLowerCase();\n22\t        return got === expected ? undefined : new Error(`EHR MCP certificate mismatch: ${got}`);\n23\t      },\n24\t    },\n25\t  });\n26\t}\n27\t\n28\ttype Token = { value: string; exp: number };\n29\tconst tokens = new Map<string, Token>();\n30\t\n31\tasync function ehrToken(clinicId: string, scope: string): Promise<string> {\n32\t  const cacheKey = `${clinicId}|${scope}`;\n33\t  const hit = tokens.get(cacheKey);\n34\t  if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;\n35\t\n36\t  const sec = await sm.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId: `clinic-agent/ehr/${clinicId}` }));\n37\t  const { client_id, client_secret, token_url } = JSON.parse(sec.SecretString ?? \"{}\");\n38\t  const res = await fetch(token_url, {\n39\t    method: \"POST\",\n40\t    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" },\n41\t    body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),\n42\t  });\n43\t  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`EHR token request failed: ${res.status}`);\n44\t  const body = (await res.json()) as { access_token: string; expires_in: number };\n45\t  tokens.set(cacheKey, { value: body.access_token, exp: Date.now() + body.expires_in * 1000 });\n46\t  return body.access_token;\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\tconst SCOPES = \"patient.read appointment.read appointment.write\";\n50\tconst sessions = new Map<string, Client>();\n51\t\n52\tasync function session(server: ConfiguredServer, clinicId: string): Promise<Client> {\n53\t  const existing = sessions.get(clinicId);\n54\t  if (existing) return existing;\n55\t  const token = await ehrToken(clinicId, SCOPES);\n56\t  const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(new URL(server.url), {\n57\t    requestInit: {\n58\t      headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \"x-clinic-id\": clinicId },\n59\t      // @ts-expect-error undici dispatcher is accepted by Node's fetch\n60\t      dispatcher: pinnedDispatcher(server),\n61\t    },\n62\t  });\n63\t  const client = new Client({ name: \"clinic-agent\", version: \"3.4.1\" });\n64\t  await client.connect(transport);\n65\t  sessions.set(clinicId, client);\n66\t  setTimeout(() => {\n67\t    sessions.delete(clinicId);\n68\t    void client.close();\n69\t  }, 4 * 60_000).unref();\n70\t  return client;\n71\t}\n72\t\n73\texport function ehr(server: ConfiguredServer) {\n74\t  return {\n75\t    async catalog(): Promise<{ reportedName?: string; meta: ServerMeta }> {\n76\t      const c = await session(server, \"_catalog\");\n77\t      const [tools, prompts, templates] = await Promise.all([\n78\t        c.listTools(),\n79\t        c.listPrompts().catch(() => ({ prompts: [] })),\n80\t        c.listResourceTemplates().catch(() => ({ resourceTemplates: [] })),\n81\t      ]);\n82\t      return {\n83\t        reportedName: c.getServerVersion()?.name,\n84\t        meta: {\n85\t          instructions: c.getInstructions(),\n86\t          tools: tools.tools as ServerMeta[\"tools\"],\n87\t          prompts: prompts.prompts as ServerMeta[\"prompts\"],\n88\t          resourceTemplates: templates.resourceTemplates as ServerMeta[\"resourceTemplates\"],\n89\t        },\n90\t      };\n91\t    },\n92\t\n93\t    async call(tool: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, opts: { clinicId: string; signal: AbortSignal }): Promise<unknown> {\n94\t      const c = await session(server, opts.clinicId);\n95\t      const res = await c.callTool({ name: tool, arguments: input }, undefined, { signal: opts.signal, timeout: 15_000 });\n96\t      if (res.isError) throw new Error(`EHR tool ${tool} returned an error`);\n97\t      return res.structuredContent ?? res.content;\n98\t    },\n99\t\n100\t    async getAppointment(clinicId: string, appointmentId: string, signal: AbortSignal) {\n101\t      return (await this.call(\"get_appointment\", { appointmentId }, { clinicId, signal })) as {\n102\t        id: string;\n103\t        patientId: string;\n104\t        start: string;\n105\t        serviceCode: string;\n106\t        payerId?: string;\n107\t        depositId?: string;\n108\t        status: string;\n109\t      };\n110\t    },\n111\t\n112\t    async appointmentsOn(clinicId: string, date: string, signal: AbortSignal) {\n113\t      return (await this.call(\"list_appointments_by_date\", { date }, { clinicId, signal })) as Array<{\n114\t        id: string;\n115\t        patientId: string;\n116\t        start: string;\n117\t        phone: string;\n118\t        smsOptIn: boolean;\n119\t        locationName: string;\n120\t      }>;\n121\t    },\n122\t  };\n123\t}\n124\texport type Ehr = ReturnType<typeof ehr>;\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b25ad3d-7d56-4f71-b8dd-d24bffe04ea7","uuid":"5975244c-27ac-4d81-b020-e0d6dcc13eb8","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:47:31.262Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-x8qeu7_i/agent/src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts","content":"import { Client } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/index.js\";\nimport { StreamableHTTPClientTransport } from \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/client/streamableHttp.js\";\nimport { GetSecretValueCommand, SecretsManagerClient } from \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\";\nimport { Agent } from \"undici\";\nimport type { PeerCertificate } from \"node:tls\";\nimport { env } from \"../config.js\";\nimport type { ConfiguredServer } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\nimport type { ServerMeta } from \"../tools/metadata-scan.js\";\n\n// EHR access goes through the EHR vendor's MCP server. Each clinic has its own OAuth client in the\n// EHR, so tokens are clinic-scoped on the EHR side. Client secrets live in Secrets Manager under\n// clinic-agent/ehr/<clinicId>; access tokens last 5 minutes and are cached until 30 s before expiry.\n\nconst sm = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: env.region });\n\nfunction pinnedDispatcher(server: ConfiguredServer): Agent {\n  const expected = server.tlsCertSha256.toLowerCase();\n  return new Agent({\n    connect: {\n      checkServerIdentity: (_host: string, cert: PeerCertificate) => {\n        const got = cert.fingerprint256.replace(/:/g, \"\").toLowerCase();\n        return got === expected ? undefined : new Error(`EHR MCP certificate mismatch: ${got}`);\n      },\n    },\n  });\n}\n\ntype Token = { value: string; exp: number };\nconst tokens = new Map<string, Token>();\n\nasync function ehrToken(clinicId: string, scope: string): Promise<string> {\n  const cacheKey = `${clinicId}|${scope}`;\n  const hit = tokens.get(cacheKey);\n  if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;\n\n  const sec = await sm.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId: `clinic-agent/ehr/${clinicId}` }));\n  const { client_id, client_secret, token_url } = JSON.parse(sec.SecretString ?? \"{}\");\n  const res = await fetch(token_url, {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" },\n    body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),\n  });\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`EHR token request failed: ${res.status}`);\n  const body = (await res.json()) as { access_token: string; expires_in: number };\n  tokens.set(cacheKey, { value: body.access_token, exp: Date.now() + body.expires_in * 1000 });\n  return body.access_token;\n}\n\nconst SCOPES = \"patient.read appointment.read appointment.write\";\nconst sessions = new Map<string, Client>();\n\nasync function session(server: ConfiguredServer, clinicId: string): Promise<Client> {\n  const existing = sessions.get(clinicId);\n  if (existing) return existing;\n  const token = await ehrToken(clinicId, SCOPES);\n  const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(new URL(server.url), {\n    requestInit: {\n      headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \"x-clinic-id\": clinicId },\n      // @ts-expect-error undici dispatcher is accepted by Node's fetch\n      dispatcher: pinnedDispatcher(server),\n    },\n  });\n  const client = new Client({ name: \"clinic-agent\", version: \"3.4.1\" });\n  await client.connect(transport);\n  sessions.set(clinicId, client);\n  setTimeout(() => {\n    sessions.delete(clinicId);\n    void client.close();\n  }, 4 * 60_000).unref();\n  return client;\n}\n\nexport function ehr(server: ConfiguredServer) {\n  return {\n    async catalog(): Promise<{ reportedName?: string; meta: ServerMeta }> {\n      const c = await session(server, \"_catalog\");\n      const [tools, prompts, templates] = await Promise.all([\n        c.listTools(),\n        c.listPrompts().catch(() => ({ prompts: [] })),\n        c.listResourceTemplates().catch(() => ({ resourceTemplates: [] })),\n      ]);\n      return {\n        reportedName: c.getServerVersion()?.name,\n        meta: {\n          instructions: c.getInstructions(),\n          tools: tools.tools as ServerMeta[\"tools\"],\n          prompts: prompts.prompts as ServerMeta[\"prompts\"],\n          resourceTemplates: templates.resourceTemplates as ServerMeta[\"resourceTemplates\"],\n        },\n      };\n    },\n\n    async call(tool: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, opts: { clinicId: string; signal: AbortSignal }): Promise<unknown> {\n      const c = await session(server, opts.clinicId);\n      const res = await c.callTool({ name: tool, arguments: input }, undefined, { signal: opts.signal, timeout: 15_000 });\n      if (res.isError) throw new Error(`EHR tool ${tool} returned an error`);\n      return res.structuredContent ?? res.content;\n    },\n\n    async getAppointment(clinicId: string, appointmentId: string, signal: AbortSignal) {\n      return (await this.call(\"get_appointment\", { appointmentId }, { clinicId, signal })) as {\n        id: string;\n        patientId: string;\n        start: string;\n        serviceCode: string;\n        payerId?: string;\n        depositId?: string;\n        status: string;\n      };\n    },\n\n    async appointmentsOn(clinicId: string, date: string, signal: AbortSignal) {\n      return (await this.call(\"list_appointments_by_date\", { date }, { clinicId, signal })) as Array<{\n        id: string;\n        patientId: string;\n        start: string;\n        phone: string;\n        smsOptIn: boolean;\n        locationName: string;\n      }>;\n    },\n  };\n}\nexport type Ehr = ReturnType<typeof ehr>;\n","numLines":125,"startLine":1,"totalLines":125}}}
